    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-12677",
      "problem": "Consider the following statement:\n\n$14$ is divisible by $4$ **or** $\\sqrt{3}$ is a rational number.\n\nWrite this statement in symbolic form using the following notations:\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14181557/assets/3ef879432a08441b6f53a10d3cb1bc7085b71c3be53c819e5dda6f7e3e085799.svg)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14181557/assets/dee5c353dfd07d9d10c79dfaf805ca7197b0afeabe307e2c369813e7121158ae.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{14 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is divisible by }\\vphantom{p} 4 }_S \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{\\sqrt{3} \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a rational number} }_T,\n$$\n\nthat is, $S \\lor T.$",
